WF-43 — Post-Consultation Handler

## Summary

- Purpose: Handles `consultation_closed` user activity. Interactive button taps route directly (done / rebook / feedback). Free-form text is classified via WF-25 (which owns the safety net), then routed: rebook → WF-45, feedback → WF-44, stop_intent → no extra (clarifier already sent by WF-25), else a grounded, topic-gated Gemini reply sent as an INTERACTIVE message that re-attaches the post-consultation buttons [Leave Feedback] [Book Again] [Done, thanks]. **Re-engaged opted-out users (`wasOptedOut=true`, set by WF-26 when an `opted_out` user is lifted to `consultation_closed` and re-routed) are handled distinctly — see D7.**
- Inputs (WF-01 canonical envelope §2.1): `phoneNumber` (top-level), `messageType` (text|interactive), `messageContent`, `rawMessage` (for interactive payloads), `wasOptedOut` (boolean — true only when WF-26 lifted this user from `opted_out` this turn), `user.{id, status, current_consultation_id, slack_channel_id}`.
- Outputs: routes to WF-44 / WF-45; a thank-you (btn_done) via WF-50 + Slack notification via WF-51; a feedback prompt; a welcome-back (re-engaged opted-out) via WF-50; or a grounded Gemini reply sent as an interactive message re-attaching the [Leave Feedback] [Book Again] [Done, thanks] buttons.
- State Transitions: none directly (downstream WFs may transition).
- Calls Sub-Workflows: WF-25 (Intent Classifier + Safety-Net Hub), WF-44 (Feedback Recorder), WF-45 (Rebook), WF-53 (U1 — on the local Gemini reply's failure), WF-61 (U2 — off-topic counting/block, safety-net §12/D6), WF-50 (Send WhatsApp), WF-51 (Send Slack — btn_done notification).
- **Deltas vs the prior WF-43 (safety-net §6, D5):**
  - stop_intent NO LONGER auto-routes to WF-47 — WF-25 sends the clarifier and returns the intent; WF-43 takes no extra action on stop_intent (removes the live inconsistency + the false-positive unsubscribe risk).
  - REMOVED the inline Gemini-error halt-and-notify chain → on the general-reply Gemini failure, call U1.
  - **D6 (safety-net §12, 2026-05-31):** the general-reply Gemini now returns JSON `{ valid_user_message, response }`. Off-topic-but-legitimate messages (`valid_user_message=false`) — which WF-25 passes through as `general_enquiry` and were previously uncounted — are now logged + counted + blockable via U2/WF-61 (`reason='off_topic'`, `blockThreshold=10`, `blockReason='threshold_off_topic'`). Parse is fail-open (malformed/missing → treat as valid). Closes the previously-unbounded off-topic cost vector without a second classify call (the response Gemini emits the relevance flag for free).
    - **Interplay with BUG-06c (§13):** D6 handles ONLY the legit pass-through buckets (`general_enquiry`/`wants_consultation`) that WF-25 returns. *Garbage* is handled + counted by WF-25 and stopped before Step 13 (WF-25 emits 0 items, §13) — so D6's off_topic check never sees garbage. The pre-§13 symptoms (a 2nd message on garbage + a null-content `off_topic` row + the garbage/off_topic double-count) are resolved by §13. The two amendments are complementary: §13 keeps garbage out; D6 counts the legit-but-off-topic remainder.
  - **D7 (re-engaged opted-out awareness, 2026-05-31):** WF-26 lifts an `opted_out` user to `consultation_closed` (no welcome message of its own — D-rule), sets `wasOptedOut=true`, and re-routes through WF-02 → WF-43. WF-43 then treated them byte-identically to a normal closed user, producing two wrong outcomes: (a) a stale **button** tap (e.g. an old `btn_done`) fired the post-consultation FAREWELL copy ("hope to see you again… reply STOP to unsubscribe") at someone who *just returned* — tonally backward; (b) a free-form **text** message got the generic returning-user Gemini reply with no acknowledgement that they had unsubscribed and are now back. D7 adds two `wasOptedOut` gates:
    - **Button path:** any button tap when `wasOptedOut=true` is *necessarily stale* (it predates the opt-out), so the button cascade is short-circuited to a single welcome-back message inviting REBOOK (Steps 3–4). Original button semantics (done/rebook/feedback) are NOT honoured for a re-engaging user — they re-enter via REBOOK.
    - **Text path:** the general-reply Gemini prompt has a `wasOptedOut=true` variant that tells the model the user previously opted out and is now resubscribed — Gemini welcomes them back AND answers/steers in ONE message (no separate send; no double-message). Both prompt variants converge on the same Gemini POST (Steps 14–17).
  - **PDF-04/05 (2026-06-06):** both general-reply prompt variants (Steps 15, 16) are now grounded in the fixed business-facts KB with the topic-gated defer rule (same KB as WF-30/31; personal astrology deferred to Dr. Chinmay; generic astrology may be answered; non-text modality → "coming soon").
  - **PDF-11 (2026-06-06):** the general-reply send (Step 21) is now an INTERACTIVE message re-attaching the three post-consultation buttons ([Leave Feedback] `btn_feedback`, [Book Again] `btn_rebook`, [Done, thanks] `btn_done`) so they don't scroll away during Q&A. Button ids are unchanged → the existing button-tap routing (Steps 2–9) is unaffected.
  - **CTA = button OR keyword (2026-06-07):** the prompts now invite the user to "tap **Book Again** below or reply **REBOOK**" — both stay valid. (Bug fixed: previously the reply told them to reply REBOOK while sending a Book Again button, mentioning only the keyword.)
  - **Time-neutral welcome (2026-06-07, Option B):** the STANDARD prompt (Step 16, normal closed user) no longer says "welcome back" — it can't know whether the user is returning minutes or days after closing, so a static welcome-back read incoherently right after a consult. Copy is now time-neutral. The OPTED-OUT variant (Step 15) KEEPS its welcome-back (a re-engaging opted-out user genuinely returned). [A gap-aware welcome via a last-contact DB lookup is deferred — post-MVP TD-NEW-042, bundles with PDF-02/03.]
- **Notes:**
  - Interactive button cascade runs only for NON-opted-out users (D7 gate at Step 3); within that, the done/rebook/feedback cascade is unchanged.
  - `wasOptedOut` is read from the trigger envelope (`$('When Executed by Another Workflow').first().json.wasOptedOut`) in both gates — robust against WF-25 dropping the field on the text path.
  - **Read-source convention (D7, 2026-05-31):** the post-Gemini consumers `Extract Gemini Reply` (phoneNumber) and `Build U2 Off-Topic Payload` (messageContent) read from the trigger node `$('When Executed by Another Workflow')`, NOT from a prompt-build node. Because Step 14 forks to one of two prompt-build nodes, the OTHER never executes that turn — any `$('Prepare Gemini Response Prompt')` reference would throw "node hasn't been executed" on the opted-out branch. The trigger node always runs and carries both fields, so it is the only safe convergence source.
  - Copy reuse-existing — verify verbatim at build.

---

## Algorithm

Step 1: Start — triggered by WF-02 for a `consultation_closed` user. Read the WF-01 canonical envelope (includes `wasOptedOut`).
Step 2: Check: `messageType == 'interactive'` (a button reply)?
  - If YES → go to Step 3.
  - If NO → go to Step 10.
Step 3: (D7 button gate) Check: `wasOptedOut === true`?
  - If YES → go to Step 4 (re-engaged opted-out user — button is stale, send welcome-back).
  - If NO → go to Step 5 (normal closed user — honour the button).
Step 4: Send the re-engagement welcome-back — call WF-50 with `{ phoneNumber, messageType: 'text', messageContent: "🙏 Welcome back to Chinmay Astro! Reply REBOOK whenever you're ready to start a new reading." }`. End.
Step 5: Inspect `rawMessage.interactive.button_reply.id`:
  - "btn_done" → go to Step 7.
  - "btn_rebook" → go to Step 6.
  - otherwise (btn_feedback or any other id) → go to Step 9.
Step 6: Call WF-45 (Rebook) with `phoneNumber`, `userId`. End.
Step 7: Send the close-thanks — call WF-50 with `{ phoneNumber, messageType: 'text', messageContent: "Thank you for choosing Chinmay Astro. We hope to see you again — just send REBOOK whenever you're ready.\n\nYou can also email chinmay_astro@gmail.com anytime if you need anything we can't help with here, or reply STOP if you'd prefer to unsubscribe." }`.
Step 8: Notify admin — call WF-51 with `{ channelId: user.slack_channel_id, messageText: "✅ User tapped \"Done, thanks\" — conversation closed. Channel stays open for any future rebook." }`. No state change. End.
Step 9: Prompt for feedback — call WF-50 with `{ phoneNumber, messageType: 'text', messageContent: "✍️ Thanks for choosing to share your feedback! Please type your thoughts about the consultation and send them — we appreciate every word!" }`. End.
Step 10: Call WF-25 with `{ phoneNumber, userId: user.id, messageContent, userStatus: user.status, userName: user.name, slackChannelId: user.slack_channel_id }`. Receive `intentResult`. **Garbage / abuse do not continue here — mechanism (BUG-06c, safety-net §13):** WF-25 emits **0 items** (its Step 13 `Return Nothing`); this handler's `Call WF-25` has `alwaysOutputData=false`, so 0 items → Step 11 onward skip. So the only intents that reach the Gemini reply (Step 16) are the pass-through buckets (`general_enquiry` / `wants_consultation`) — NOT garbage. Before BUG-06c, WF-25 returned 1 item on garbage and this handler wrongly ran its Gemini reply on it (2nd message + a null-content `off_topic` count). Do not remove WF-25's `Return Nothing`. (Gemini-failure still terminates via U1's halt.)
Step 11: Check: `intentResult == 'stop_intent'`?
  - If YES → End (WF-25 already sent the clarifier; no extra — D5).
  - If NO → go to Step 12.
Step 12: Check: `intentResult == 'rebook_intent'`?
  - If YES → call WF-45 (Rebook) with `phoneNumber`, `userId`. End.
  - If NO → go to Step 13.
Step 13: Check: `intentResult == 'feedback_intent'`?
  - If YES → call WF-44 (Feedback Recorder) with `phoneNumber`, `userId`, `messageContent`. End.
  - If NO → go to Step 14.
Step 14: (D7 text gate) Check: `wasOptedOut === true`?
  - If YES → go to Step 15 (build the opted-out-aware prompt variant).
  - If NO → go to Step 16 (build the standard prompt).
Step 15: Build the OPTED-OUT general-reply Gemini prompt — identical JSON mandate + grounded KB + topic-gated defer rule as Step 16, EXCEPT the context sentence tells the model this person previously opted out of messages and has now re-engaged (they are resubscribed): **warmly welcome them back** AND, in the same reply, answer any genuine question briefly (per the KB/topic-gate) or invite them to "tap **Book Again** below or reply **REBOOK**" for a new ₹500 reading. Emits `geminiPrompt` (same field/shape as Step 16). Go to Step 17.
Step 16: Build the STANDARD general-reply Gemini prompt — OPENS with the JSON mandate `{ valid_user_message, response }` (front-loaded for determinism, D6c), then the grounded business-facts KB (offering = text-based WhatsApp consultation; ₹500; one question/topic; audio/video coming soon; a new consultation is booked via REBOOK) with the topic-gated defer rule (greeting → warm reply; KB question → answer from KB; generic/educational astrology → may answer; a question about THIS person's chart/predictions/life/remedies → defer with "That's something Dr. Chinmay will look into for you during your consultation."; off-topic-but-legitimate → set `valid_user_message=false`, gently acknowledge + steer back). **Time-neutral (2026-06-07):** does NOT say "welcome back" (can't know elapsed time since close). To start a new reading, the copy invites the user to "tap **Book Again** below or reply **REBOOK**". Never tell a closed user to "confirm payment". Append the user's message. Emits `geminiPrompt`. Go to Step 17.
Step 17: POST the built prompt to Gemini (gemini-2.5-flash-lite, temperature=0.3, `generationConfig.responseMimeType='application/json'`). Both prompt variants (Steps 15, 16) converge here — exactly one item arrives, so the single-input HTTP node fires once. On Gemini API failure → go to Step 22. On success → go to Step 18.
Step 18: Parse the JSON response into `{ valid_user_message, response }`. **Fail-open (D6e):** if parsing fails or either field is missing/malformed, set `valid_user_message=true` and `response=` best-effort text (or a safe default welcome-back reply). Never block or silence a user on a parse glitch.
Step 19: Check: `valid_user_message === false`?
  - If NO (true / fail-open) → go to Step 21 (send the reply).
  - If YES → go to Step 20.
Step 20: (off-topic — count + block check, D6) Call U2/WF-61 with `{ phoneNumber, messageType: 'text', reason: 'off_topic', messageContent, blockThreshold: 10, blockReason: 'threshold_off_topic' }`. Receive `{ blocked }`.
  - If `blocked === true` → End (silent — U2 already set `status=blocked` and sent the admin block alert; no reply, D6a).
  - If `blocked === false` → go to Step 21 (still send the graceful redirect reply, D6a).
Step 21: Send the reply as an INTERACTIVE message — call WF-50 with `{ phoneNumber, messageType: 'interactive', interactivePayload: { type:'button', body:{ text: <response> }, action:{ buttons:[ {id:'btn_feedback', title:'Leave Feedback'}, {id:'btn_rebook', title:'Book Again'}, {id:'btn_done', title:'Done, thanks'} ] } } }`. (Re-attaches the post-consultation buttons so they don't scroll away; reached by both the valid reply and the off-topic-but-not-blocked redirect.) End.
Step 22: Gemini API failure — call U1 with `{ phoneNumber, userFacing: true, consultChannelId: user.slack_channel_id, context: { source: 'WF-43', userName: user.name, userStateText: 'consultation completed', userMessage: messageContent, errorDetail: <summary> } }`. End.
